1
00:00:04,804 --> 00:00:07,040
<i>I must do what I need to do.</i>

2
00:00:09,376 --> 00:00:11,945
<i>I cannot forgive anyone who threatens</i>

3
00:00:13,046 --> 00:00:14,214
<i>Mariko's happiness…</i>

4
00:00:15,148 --> 00:00:17,751
<i>I looked into you too, you know.</i>

5
00:00:17,817 --> 00:00:20,653
What are you to Mariko?

6
00:00:21,421 --> 00:00:23,423
<i>…because I'm the only one</i>
<i>by Mariko's side,</i>

7
00:00:24,958 --> 00:00:25,792
<i>protecting her.</i>

8
00:00:34,034 --> 00:00:36,036
Don't just stand there. Have a seat.

9
00:00:37,871 --> 00:00:39,906
-I'll make us some tea.
-That's all right.

10
00:00:40,473 --> 00:00:42,142
Don't be like that.

11
00:00:43,009 --> 00:00:44,677
These are very fine tea leaves.

12
00:00:44,744 --> 00:00:46,546
PROFILE

13
00:00:46,613 --> 00:00:50,050
Your parents' home is very close to ours.

14
00:00:50,750 --> 00:00:55,321
3-4-8 Kita-Okamoto, Setagaya Ward, Tokyo.

15
00:00:56,456 --> 00:01:00,493
You're the same age as Mariko, went to
the same schools as her, even university.

16
00:01:00,560 --> 00:01:02,996
And to top it off,
you both joined Nose Cosmetics.

17
00:01:05,732 --> 00:01:09,235
So, what instructions did Mariko give you?

18
00:01:10,437 --> 00:01:14,307
That girl acts like she has
no interest in company politics.

19
00:01:14,808 --> 00:01:17,977
Yet she quietly had her childhood friend
placed right by her side.

20
00:01:18,478 --> 00:01:19,979
I wonder what she's planning.

21
00:01:24,851 --> 00:01:26,052
Oh, I'm sorry.

22
00:01:26,586 --> 00:01:29,722
Hearing you say "childhood friend"…

23
00:01:31,724 --> 00:01:33,226
What? That's creepy.

24
00:01:36,930 --> 00:01:38,798
I heard something very interesting.

25
00:01:38,865 --> 00:01:40,033
COMPANY PROBLEMS
A FACE SHROUDED IN DARKNESS

26
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:41,901
It seems you're currently under suspicion.

27
00:01:43,636 --> 00:01:44,904
Then I got it.

28
00:01:46,306 --> 00:01:49,142
It was also you who sent this
to my husband, right?

29
00:01:51,578 --> 00:01:53,580
<i>Tateiwa truly was hopeless.</i>

30
00:01:53,646 --> 00:01:54,547
<i>Engaging in such petty misconduct.</i>

31
00:01:57,050 --> 00:02:02,122
You were in the accounting department
from 2018 to 2021, right?

32
00:02:02,188 --> 00:02:04,724
And after that,
the IT promotion department?

33
00:02:05,325 --> 00:02:07,694
I heard you were extremely competent.

34
00:02:09,362 --> 00:02:13,299
Illegally accessing the accounting system
to retrieve data should be easy enough

35
00:02:13,366 --> 00:02:15,101
for someone like you, wouldn't it?

36
00:02:17,170 --> 00:02:20,573
Say, why don't you join my side?

37
00:02:22,342 --> 00:02:24,544
I would love an underling like you.

38
00:02:25,512 --> 00:02:29,182
You can keep pretending to be
Mariko's ally just like before,

39
00:02:29,682 --> 00:02:32,051
as long as you also do what I ask.

40
00:02:32,719 --> 00:02:34,787
-What you ask?
-Yes.

41
00:02:35,355 --> 00:02:37,290
That girl is an eyesore.

42
00:02:38,091 --> 00:02:41,327
Her mother died so easily
and gave up her position.

43
00:02:42,328 --> 00:02:44,964
But in that regard,
she's not like her mother at all.

44
00:02:47,300 --> 00:02:49,903
I'll prepare a suitable position
for you as well.

45
00:02:51,037 --> 00:02:52,939
Far better than staying
attached to Mariko--

46
00:03:01,214 --> 00:03:02,215
I'm sorry.

47
00:03:12,759 --> 00:03:13,626
No, so…

48
00:03:15,595 --> 00:03:17,564
You've completely misunderstood
the situation.

49
00:03:19,199 --> 00:03:22,302
I haven't been taking
any instructions from Mariko.

50
00:03:24,070 --> 00:03:26,706
Mariko is an upright person
with a strong sense of justice,

51
00:03:26,773 --> 00:03:29,075
so she would never use
underhanded methods like you.

52
00:03:30,276 --> 00:03:33,546
<i>She earns what she wants</i>
<i>through hard work, fairly and squarely.</i>

53
00:03:34,881 --> 00:03:36,649
And I also won't forgive you

54
00:03:37,483 --> 00:03:39,919
if you try to scheme
against Mariko any further.

55
00:03:42,422 --> 00:03:45,491
What? Are you saying you're doing
all this of your own will?

56
00:03:47,760 --> 00:03:50,296
So even Mariko doesn't know about this?

57
00:03:53,066 --> 00:03:54,934
About this background of yours?

58
00:03:56,970 --> 00:03:59,606
What is this? How creepy!

59
00:03:59,672 --> 00:04:02,408
-Are you her stalker or something?
-Stalker?

60
00:04:02,475 --> 00:04:05,378
-Me?
-Well, of course.

61
00:04:05,445 --> 00:04:07,413
You're this obsessed with her.

62
00:04:10,717 --> 00:04:13,219
I wonder how Mariko
would feel if she found out.

63
00:04:17,323 --> 00:04:18,558
Do as you wish.

64
00:04:19,325 --> 00:04:22,895
My background is something
anyone can find, like you did.

65
00:04:24,130 --> 00:04:26,065
But I'm certain you won't tell her.

66
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:30,303
After all, if your own actions
were exposed, you have far more to lose.

67
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:41,481
<i>Around every bright light,</i>

68
00:04:42,315 --> 00:04:45,451
<i>there are always annoying bugs, swarming.</i>

69
00:04:51,157 --> 00:04:53,059
YUKIMURA

70
00:04:53,126 --> 00:04:55,995
SOTA YUKIMURA

71
00:04:56,062 --> 00:04:58,197
YUKI<i>SONO</i>2199

72
00:05:00,400 --> 00:05:02,001
<i>You do not need to know.</i>

73
00:05:07,140 --> 00:05:10,777
<i>It's fine. I know how…</i>

74
00:05:13,913 --> 00:05:15,014
<i>to protect Mariko.</i>

75
00:05:24,357 --> 00:05:26,392
‎REGARDING WHAT I ASKED YOU FOR

76
00:05:30,730 --> 00:05:32,098
A private investigation agency?

77
00:05:32,865 --> 00:05:33,966
I'm back!

78
00:05:34,634 --> 00:05:37,370
Were you able to restore the PC data
from Tateiwa's secondary residence?

79
00:05:37,437 --> 00:05:39,505
Yes, I'm checking it out right now.

80
00:05:40,940 --> 00:05:44,377
There's a lot of shady stuff on here.

81
00:05:45,044 --> 00:05:47,280
Lots of internal company data.

82
00:05:47,347 --> 00:05:53,486
Did he intend to prepare all this
and stage an internal coup?

83
00:05:54,354 --> 00:05:56,956
Which means it was probably
someone from the company.

84
00:05:57,023 --> 00:06:00,693
Those expense fraud documents
sent to the president

85
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:02,395
also seem like the work of an insider.

86
00:06:03,296 --> 00:06:05,164
Can we see where it was sent from?

87
00:06:05,231 --> 00:06:07,233
Well, it's tough at the moment.

88
00:06:07,900 --> 00:06:11,437
I think it's someone
who's very well-versed in tech.

89
00:06:18,177 --> 00:06:21,114
Sota Yukimura would be able
to do that, right?

90
00:06:21,180 --> 00:06:23,182
He came from the IT department
and was quite capable.

91
00:06:23,249 --> 00:06:25,551
Those skills would come in handy.

92
00:06:26,819 --> 00:06:29,088
But we don't know the motive.

93
00:06:29,789 --> 00:06:34,427
First, we want to know if that DNA found
at Tateiwa's murder scene the other day

94
00:06:35,094 --> 00:06:38,097
belongs to Yukimura.

95
00:06:38,798 --> 00:06:43,035
Can't we make up a reason to bring him in,
then test his DNA?

96
00:06:43,102 --> 00:06:44,137
That would be problematic.

97
00:06:45,371 --> 00:06:48,574
What reason? We found nothing else
regarding Yukimura, right?

98
00:06:49,642 --> 00:06:51,077
Well, yes.

99
00:06:52,078 --> 00:06:55,181
Even if the DNA belongs to Yukimura,

100
00:06:55,248 --> 00:06:56,949
he already admitted himself that he met

101
00:06:57,016 --> 00:06:59,318
Tateiwa at the scene
right before he was killed.

102
00:07:00,253 --> 00:07:03,222
In that case, it wouldn't be strange
for his DNA to be left at the scene.

103
00:07:03,289 --> 00:07:04,957
-But Kajiwara--
-More importantly…

104
00:07:05,024 --> 00:07:06,292
Oh, yes.

105
00:07:06,359 --> 00:07:09,529
At 1:15 p.m. the day after
the body was discovered,

106
00:07:09,595 --> 00:07:12,465
this was caught on CCTV
at Tateiwa's secondary apartment.

107
00:07:13,099 --> 00:07:16,269
If this person deleted the data…

108
00:07:16,335 --> 00:07:18,504
There's a high probability
they know something.

109
00:07:19,272 --> 00:07:21,007
Identify them immediately
and look into them.

110
00:07:21,073 --> 00:07:22,008
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

111
00:07:22,074 --> 00:07:24,210
-Let's go. You and you, come with me.
-Yes, sir.

112
00:07:24,277 --> 00:07:25,578
-We'll go to the scene first.
-Yes, sir.

113
00:07:44,230 --> 00:07:49,035
<i>Lately I've had to think</i>
<i>about Mariko so much</i>

114
00:07:49,101 --> 00:07:51,204
<i>that my head feels like</i>
<i>it's about to explode.</i>

115
00:07:58,978 --> 00:08:02,448
<i>Mariko's safety and smile</i>
<i>matter more than anything else.</i>

116
00:08:06,319 --> 00:08:07,553
<i>And yet…</i>

117
00:08:15,094 --> 00:08:17,864
<i>Why did I end up saying something so bold?</i>

118
00:08:19,232 --> 00:08:21,467
What makes you like that person so much?

119
00:08:22,468 --> 00:08:25,204
Her sense of justice, I suppose.

120
00:08:26,606 --> 00:08:28,407
She's my hero.

121
00:08:31,344 --> 00:08:34,580
<i>She definitely realized</i>
<i>I was talking about her.</i>

122
00:08:35,748 --> 00:08:39,886
<i>How am I supposed</i>
<i>to face Mariko going forward?</i>

123
00:08:40,720 --> 00:08:41,988
Do you like that one?

124
00:08:42,922 --> 00:08:43,923
It's cute, isn't it?

125
00:08:44,657 --> 00:08:45,491
Yes.

126
00:08:46,125 --> 00:08:48,060
Looking at it makes me feel at ease.

127
00:08:48,661 --> 00:08:49,495
Take your time.

128
00:08:55,234 --> 00:08:57,169
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

129
00:08:58,070 --> 00:09:01,173
-Good morning.
-Yukimura, I know you just got here,

130
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:02,742
but check this for me.

131
00:09:02,808 --> 00:09:03,843
Yes.

132
00:09:04,443 --> 00:09:06,712
If there are no issues,
just leave it at the usual spot.

133
00:09:07,980 --> 00:09:08,981
Understood.

134
00:09:18,424 --> 00:09:19,292
<i>Huh?</i>

135
00:09:20,092 --> 00:09:22,194
<i>She's acting as if</i>
<i>nothing happened at all.</i>

136
00:09:25,231 --> 00:09:27,867
<i>It really is as if nothing happened.</i>

137
00:09:29,435 --> 00:09:30,369
<i>Huh?</i>

138
00:09:31,170 --> 00:09:33,606
<i>Wait, did Mariko not realize</i>
<i>that I was talking about her?</i>

139
00:09:35,641 --> 00:09:36,609
<i>Wait, hold on!</i>

140
00:09:36,676 --> 00:09:39,345
What is it? That's scary.

141
00:09:39,412 --> 00:09:40,279
A-Are you okay?

142
00:09:41,414 --> 00:09:43,783
Yes, I'm sorry.

143
00:09:48,554 --> 00:09:52,692
<i>I've finally realized something crucial.</i>

144
00:10:02,301 --> 00:10:06,806
There was no way Mariko would think
those words were directed at her.

145
00:10:07,807 --> 00:10:08,674
Why?

146
00:10:09,809 --> 00:10:13,713
Mariko believes I have had someone
I liked for a very long time.

147
00:10:16,916 --> 00:10:17,950
Wait, so what?

148
00:10:18,684 --> 00:10:21,320
I mean someone I've liked for a long time!

149
00:10:23,222 --> 00:10:25,358
-Ah!
-Don't "ah" me.

150
00:10:25,858 --> 00:10:27,793
Besides, the more seriously

151
00:10:27,860 --> 00:10:29,996
I talk about my feelings for this person
I've liked for a long time,

152
00:10:30,630 --> 00:10:33,599
the further I fall
out of Mariko's romantic consideration.

153
00:10:35,001 --> 00:10:37,303
Wait, why?

154
00:10:39,672 --> 00:10:41,841
He has someone he's liked for a long time?

155
00:10:42,775 --> 00:10:43,609
Yes.

156
00:10:43,676 --> 00:10:47,446
So, I won't be pursuing him.

157
00:10:48,714 --> 00:10:50,783
Wait a second.

158
00:10:50,850 --> 00:10:53,619
Even assuming Yukimura has someone
he's liked for a long time--

159
00:10:53,686 --> 00:10:55,421
He does.

160
00:10:55,488 --> 00:10:58,224
Why do you have to stop pursuing him?

161
00:10:59,925 --> 00:11:02,828
Who he likes is his business!

162
00:11:02,895 --> 00:11:04,230
What about your feelings, Mariko?

163
00:11:06,432 --> 00:11:08,901
Besides, it's not like that person
is his girlfriend yet, right?

164
00:11:08,968 --> 00:11:10,803
Is there a problem with that?

165
00:11:14,507 --> 00:11:16,442
I don't like that kind of situation.

166
00:11:17,309 --> 00:11:18,144
Hm?

167
00:11:18,978 --> 00:11:24,784
When I date someone, I want to build
a relationship with a future in mind.

168
00:11:25,985 --> 00:11:30,723
So I don't want a one-sided,
unrequited love.

169
00:11:32,324 --> 00:11:36,495
I mean, falling for someone
who already likes someone else

170
00:11:36,562 --> 00:11:40,232
is basically hoping they
and the other person will drift apart.

171
00:11:46,038 --> 00:11:48,040
He's a bit unusual,
but he's a good person,

172
00:11:49,475 --> 00:11:51,177
so I hope things go well for him.

173
00:11:54,180 --> 00:11:57,550
I could really tell how much
he likes that girl,

174
00:11:59,418 --> 00:12:01,987
and it felt like true love…

175
00:12:04,957 --> 00:12:07,593
which I thought was wonderful.

176
00:12:13,099 --> 00:12:16,836
No, uh, besides, I didn't
like him in the first place.

177
00:12:20,339 --> 00:12:22,141
This is because you ran
your mouth, Tomoya.

178
00:12:22,742 --> 00:12:23,909
Me?

179
00:12:24,944 --> 00:12:25,878
Me, huh?

180
00:12:28,781 --> 00:12:31,383
Still, depending on how you look at it,
this is an opportunity.

181
00:12:36,422 --> 00:12:37,456
I mean…

182
00:12:38,157 --> 00:12:40,526
You can just start talking

183
00:12:40,593 --> 00:12:43,796
-to her more from now on.
-You always say the exact same thing.

184
00:12:44,530 --> 00:12:47,166
No, I really think this is your chance.

185
00:12:48,134 --> 00:12:51,737
She already knows
you have someone you like,

186
00:12:51,804 --> 00:12:54,640
and she understands
that your feelings are serious.

187
00:12:54,707 --> 00:12:56,742
Then all you have to do
is tell her that it's her.

188
00:12:56,809 --> 00:12:59,612
-Just say it, you got it!
-There's no way I can say that.

189
00:13:00,246 --> 00:13:01,080
Why?

190
00:13:02,414 --> 00:13:05,417
There's no way I can tell her
I've liked her for a long time.

191
00:13:06,085 --> 00:13:07,286
Really?

192
00:13:08,154 --> 00:13:09,255
Well, that kind of thing…

193
00:13:11,157 --> 00:13:12,358
I guess it's creepy, huh?

194
00:13:38,417 --> 00:13:39,952
The progress…

195
00:13:41,187 --> 00:13:42,154
Yes, this.

196
00:13:46,225 --> 00:13:48,260
It's fine, it's fine. It'll work.

197
00:13:48,828 --> 00:13:50,229
It'll work. It's fine.

198
00:14:07,313 --> 00:14:10,716
What? Even you only got an email
from Asai, President?

199
00:14:10,783 --> 00:14:14,186
Yes. He has never taken
time off like this before,

200
00:14:14,253 --> 00:14:17,056
so I got worried that something
might have happened.

201
00:14:22,561 --> 00:14:25,364
Notifications went out to both
the secretarial section and HR,

202
00:14:25,431 --> 00:14:27,766
so procedurally, there's no issue, but…

203
00:14:27,833 --> 00:14:28,667
Indeed.

204
00:14:28,734 --> 00:14:31,003
He's not answering his phone either.

205
00:14:32,104 --> 00:14:34,907
Given the timing,
I'm concerned about a few things.

206
00:14:35,574 --> 00:14:37,776
Do you mean the Tateiwa case?

207
00:14:37,843 --> 00:14:38,677
Yes.

208
00:14:38,744 --> 00:14:42,114
If he happened to get
caught up in some incident…

209
00:14:44,216 --> 00:14:48,687
We also have to consider the culprit
behind Mariko's kidnapping.

210
00:14:49,688 --> 00:14:53,759
That Hatano man has been
talking to weekly magazines.

211
00:14:54,360 --> 00:14:55,828
What could he be aiming for?

212
00:14:56,896 --> 00:14:59,198
If he were to make contact with Mariko--

213
00:14:59,265 --> 00:15:01,233
That's what worries me as well.

214
00:15:02,568 --> 00:15:05,537
Please continue to look after Mariko.

215
00:15:05,604 --> 00:15:07,539
Report to me whenever anything comes up.

216
00:15:08,374 --> 00:15:09,475
Understood.

217
00:15:23,222 --> 00:15:25,190
Did Sota Yukimura
really have no interaction

218
00:15:25,257 --> 00:15:28,460
with Mariko before he
transferred departments?

219
00:15:29,128 --> 00:15:31,196
Yes, that appears to be the case.

220
00:15:31,764 --> 00:15:34,233
Is that man Mariko's stalker?

221
00:15:37,036 --> 00:15:38,537
He was strangely composed

222
00:15:39,305 --> 00:15:41,206
and eerie.

223
00:15:42,641 --> 00:15:45,144
It seems likely he's hiding
other things as well.

224
00:15:45,878 --> 00:15:47,579
He's definitely scheming something.

225
00:15:47,646 --> 00:15:49,014
But more importantly,

226
00:15:50,950 --> 00:15:53,719
do we have any information we can use?

227
00:15:54,486 --> 00:15:56,922
My apologies. Nothing at the moment.

228
00:15:59,158 --> 00:16:01,160
You're useless.

229
00:16:05,030 --> 00:16:09,001
Yukimura has a weak presence
at the company,

230
00:16:09,601 --> 00:16:11,737
but he's a hard worker and thoughtful,

231
00:16:12,638 --> 00:16:15,207
so he's liked by those
who have worked with him.

232
00:16:18,310 --> 00:16:20,412
-And?
-I'm sorry.

233
00:16:20,479 --> 00:16:22,581
Ah, changing the subject,

234
00:16:23,182 --> 00:16:26,218
the president called in
Mariko's subordinate, Izumi,

235
00:16:26,285 --> 00:16:28,887
and instructed her to look into Asai.

236
00:16:29,488 --> 00:16:31,056
It seems that the president

237
00:16:31,123 --> 00:16:34,059
may be hiding something with Asai--

238
00:16:34,126 --> 00:16:36,895
That's fine. I don't care about Asai.

239
00:16:38,163 --> 00:16:41,600
If you learn anything new about
Sota Yukimura, report to me immediately.

240
00:16:42,735 --> 00:16:45,170
Yes. Excuse me.

241
00:17:10,763 --> 00:17:12,965
WHEN TO CONFESS

242
00:17:13,031 --> 00:17:16,335
THE TIMING TO CONFESS…

243
00:17:36,422 --> 00:17:37,623
I told you I didn't need any.

244
00:17:40,359 --> 00:17:43,729
However, since you brewed it,
I'll take it.

245
00:17:59,244 --> 00:18:00,179
Is this the usual one?

246
00:18:00,245 --> 00:18:03,582
Oh, no, since it's nighttime,
I made it decaf.

247
00:18:05,117 --> 00:18:08,787
You're too thoughtful, anticipating
things way too far in advance,

248
00:18:08,854 --> 00:18:09,955
it's scary.

249
00:18:11,423 --> 00:18:12,558
I'm sorry.

250
00:18:12,624 --> 00:18:15,260
You don't need to go that far.
Just being normal is fine.

251
00:18:15,327 --> 00:18:16,195
Okay.

252
00:18:18,997 --> 00:18:20,933
Oh, but thank you.

253
00:18:31,577 --> 00:18:33,011
-Ah, um…
-Ah, um…

254
00:18:37,449 --> 00:18:39,818
-Go ahead.
-No, go ahead.

255
00:18:41,186 --> 00:18:44,323
Oh, uh…

256
00:18:46,325 --> 00:18:48,894
-I need to ask you something.
-Yes?

257
00:18:51,130 --> 00:18:52,898
Where are you from, Yukimura?

258
00:18:55,467 --> 00:18:57,102
Tokyo.

259
00:18:57,870 --> 00:18:59,505
Where in Tokyo?

260
00:19:01,140 --> 00:19:03,842
Around Setagaya.

261
00:19:03,909 --> 00:19:05,177
Where in Setagaya?

262
00:19:10,949 --> 00:19:14,786
Around Kita-Okamoto and that area.

263
00:19:15,954 --> 00:19:17,256
Oh, right near my home…

264
00:19:18,657 --> 00:19:20,959
Your middle school and high school
were around there, too?

265
00:19:21,026 --> 00:19:22,327
No, back then…

266
00:19:27,633 --> 00:19:28,867
Yes, they were.

267
00:19:28,934 --> 00:19:31,703
When you were a child,
where did you go for summer festivals?

268
00:19:31,770 --> 00:19:33,939
-The ones nearby--
-Why are you asking all of a sudden?

269
00:19:34,706 --> 00:19:37,042
Oh, no reason…

270
00:19:39,077 --> 00:19:42,981
Did someone perhaps say something to you?

271
00:19:43,849 --> 00:19:46,185
Oh, no…

272
00:19:47,553 --> 00:19:48,554
I just…

273
00:19:49,555 --> 00:19:50,389
<i>Excuse me!</i>

274
00:19:51,790 --> 00:19:54,126
FESTIVAL

275
00:19:59,364 --> 00:20:01,500
<i>It was popular back when</i>
<i>I was in middle school.</i>

276
00:20:01,567 --> 00:20:03,969
Once I like something,
I tend to stay attached to it forever.

277
00:20:04,536 --> 00:20:06,205
I still use it.

278
00:20:10,275 --> 00:20:11,910
Guess there's no way…

279
00:20:14,346 --> 00:20:16,281
There couldn't be such a coincidence…

280
00:20:17,749 --> 00:20:19,718
-Sorry, it's nothing.
-Huh?

281
00:20:21,153 --> 00:20:22,421
What about you?

282
00:20:24,690 --> 00:20:26,525
-Ah…
-You were about to say something, right?

283
00:20:26,592 --> 00:20:27,593
Never mind, actually.

284
00:20:27,659 --> 00:20:30,295
-Never mind? What is it? I'm curious.
-No.

285
00:20:31,530 --> 00:20:32,364
Really, it's nothing.

286
00:20:53,885 --> 00:20:56,622
MARIKO NOSE

287
00:21:00,125 --> 00:21:02,628
Hey, can I throw this away?

288
00:21:02,694 --> 00:21:05,163
Oh, sorry, sorry.

289
00:21:06,632 --> 00:21:07,599
What? No…

290
00:21:08,600 --> 00:21:10,369
Why did I do something like this?

291
00:21:12,471 --> 00:21:14,406
Manager, you were reading
this document here earlier, right?

292
00:21:15,774 --> 00:21:17,943
Since it was a hassle to get sticky notes,

293
00:21:18,010 --> 00:21:21,546
you just wedged it in whatever, but then
you had an idea, so you left it there.

294
00:21:22,414 --> 00:21:24,916
Like I said, stop doing that stuff.

295
00:21:24,983 --> 00:21:26,084
Why am I getting scolded?

296
00:21:26,151 --> 00:21:28,854
Because the way you act,

297
00:21:28,920 --> 00:21:31,156
like you understand everything,
it is just annoying.

298
00:21:32,257 --> 00:21:33,659
Are you a psychic?

299
00:21:33,725 --> 00:21:36,194
Um, with all due respect,

300
00:21:36,261 --> 00:21:38,864
I think anyone could figure this out.
You're usually like this, Manager.

301
00:21:38,930 --> 00:21:40,799
That's not true! This was just by chance.

302
00:21:41,800 --> 00:21:42,634
Oh.

303
00:21:44,403 --> 00:21:48,240
The other day, some coffee was left
in the coffee machine.

304
00:21:48,907 --> 00:21:50,609
You probably received a sudden phone call.

305
00:21:50,676 --> 00:21:53,111
There was also a time a rice ball was left

306
00:21:53,178 --> 00:21:55,447
in the meeting room
for several hours, you know?

307
00:22:01,453 --> 00:22:05,223
It just made me think about how
absorbed in your work you get.

308
00:22:06,792 --> 00:22:07,826
Annoying!

309
00:22:09,428 --> 00:22:11,663
What's with you acting
like you're the only reliable one?

310
00:22:16,968 --> 00:22:17,803
Huh?

311
00:22:20,639 --> 00:22:21,873
Wait, wait…

312
00:22:23,275 --> 00:22:24,242
Wait…

313
00:22:29,715 --> 00:22:31,249
You're laughing too much.

314
00:22:40,992 --> 00:22:42,561
I should be heading home soon.

315
00:22:51,570 --> 00:22:53,138
<i>Things are fine just as they are.</i>

316
00:22:56,708 --> 00:22:59,311
I couldn't imagine
being able to talk to her like this

317
00:22:59,378 --> 00:23:00,579
until recently.

318
00:23:04,149 --> 00:23:06,351
So this is fine.

319
00:23:09,488 --> 00:23:11,790
If I say it, I might lose everything.

320
00:23:15,460 --> 00:23:16,795
I prefer what I have now.

321
00:23:47,125 --> 00:23:48,393
Mariko.

322
00:23:48,460 --> 00:23:51,163
-Yes?
-Do you like amusement parks?

323
00:23:52,631 --> 00:23:54,466
-What? Amusement parks?
-Yes.

324
00:23:55,567 --> 00:23:58,837
I don't think I've been to one
since middle school.

325
00:23:59,471 --> 00:24:01,106
That was a really long time ago.

326
00:24:02,073 --> 00:24:05,677
Oh… I end up having
too much time on my hands.

327
00:24:06,478 --> 00:24:07,446
What do you mean?

328
00:24:09,881 --> 00:24:11,383
We can ride together actually.

329
00:24:11,450 --> 00:24:13,118
-What? We can?
-What? That's awesome.

330
00:24:13,185 --> 00:24:15,220
Really? Yay, yay!

331
00:24:15,287 --> 00:24:17,122
-Wow.
-This is crazy!

332
00:24:17,189 --> 00:24:19,291
-Next, please.
-Let's go, let's go.

333
00:24:20,225 --> 00:24:21,393
It's written right there.

334
00:24:21,460 --> 00:24:24,229
-Really? You can't shake it?
-Stop it.

335
00:24:24,296 --> 00:24:25,430
Guys, it won't shake.

336
00:24:25,497 --> 00:24:27,399
<i>It's time spent</i>
<i>doing nothing in particular.</i>

337
00:24:27,466 --> 00:24:30,302
I don't really know
what I'm supposed to enjoy…

338
00:24:30,368 --> 00:24:31,703
Wow…

339
00:24:32,571 --> 00:24:36,274
Well, it also depends
on who you go with, though.

340
00:24:39,544 --> 00:24:42,414
So, what about this amusement park?

341
00:24:42,481 --> 00:24:45,550
Well, Sara keeps saying she wants to go,

342
00:24:45,617 --> 00:24:48,587
but I'm unsure if we should go alone.

343
00:24:48,653 --> 00:24:50,388
Sure, I'll go with you.

344
00:24:50,455 --> 00:24:52,090
-No, it's fine.
-What, why?

345
00:24:52,157 --> 00:24:53,325
-I don't mind at all.
-No.

346
00:24:53,391 --> 00:24:55,093
I'd feel awkward.

347
00:24:55,160 --> 00:24:56,261
It's fine, it's fine.

348
00:24:59,197 --> 00:25:04,469
I mean, I wondered how a double date
with the two of us and my kid would be,

349
00:25:04,536 --> 00:25:06,571
-but I guess it's impossible…
-What?

350
00:25:06,638 --> 00:25:09,407
Is there anything else? An aquarium?

351
00:25:18,917 --> 00:25:21,987
‎METROPOLITAN ART CANVAS

352
00:25:31,296 --> 00:25:33,999
-Sorry to keep you waiting.
-No, not at all.

353
00:25:34,065 --> 00:25:36,902
I'm the one who invited you
so suddenly, after all.

354
00:25:37,602 --> 00:25:38,436
No…

355
00:25:39,037 --> 00:25:40,805
-Here.
-Thank you.

356
00:25:40,872 --> 00:25:41,973
VINCENT WALLACE

357
00:25:42,841 --> 00:25:43,708
This way.

358
00:25:48,980 --> 00:25:50,949
Are you interested in paintings and art?

359
00:25:51,850 --> 00:25:54,786
Yes, although I'm not
very knowledgeable about them.

360
00:25:54,853 --> 00:25:56,221
That's great.

361
00:25:57,389 --> 00:25:59,124
Do you often go see them?

362
00:26:01,092 --> 00:26:04,963
Since that kind of knowledge
might prove useful for work someday,

363
00:26:05,030 --> 00:26:07,198
I try to go whenever I have time.

364
00:26:08,567 --> 00:26:09,935
You're very dedicated to your work.

365
00:26:11,503 --> 00:26:15,040
No, uh, it's actually not a good thing.

366
00:26:15,840 --> 00:26:17,309
I realized it as I said it out loud.

367
00:26:18,510 --> 00:26:19,678
Why not?

368
00:26:19,744 --> 00:26:23,081
I'm consuming art based
on calculations of gain and loss.

369
00:26:27,319 --> 00:26:28,620
I think that's fine.

370
00:26:29,321 --> 00:26:30,956
Everyone has their own perspective.

371
00:26:37,696 --> 00:26:39,664
My mother used to say
something in the past.

372
00:26:41,666 --> 00:26:42,701
Your mother?

373
00:26:43,301 --> 00:26:44,836
My mother liked paintings.

374
00:26:47,472 --> 00:26:49,941
She would stare at the exact
same painting for a long time,

375
00:26:50,842 --> 00:26:53,912
so I once asked her why she
kept looking at only that one.

376
00:26:55,680 --> 00:26:56,715
And she said,

377
00:26:58,183 --> 00:27:01,152
"For some reason,
my heart is drawn to this.

378
00:27:02,320 --> 00:27:06,024
I feel like I really love it."

379
00:27:08,393 --> 00:27:11,730
I want to have that kind of feeling too.

380
00:27:13,832 --> 00:27:15,667
It doesn't matter
if I don't understand why.

381
00:27:16,301 --> 00:27:18,169
Just that my heart is drawn to it.

382
00:27:22,407 --> 00:27:24,509
It's interesting talking to you, Mariko.

383
00:27:25,844 --> 00:27:28,146
You hold values
that are different from mine.

384
00:27:33,918 --> 00:27:36,888
Do you go to art museums often, Sakura?

385
00:27:37,822 --> 00:27:38,823
Yes.

386
00:27:40,358 --> 00:27:44,663
I actually used to want
to become a painter.

387
00:27:45,363 --> 00:27:47,565
-Is that so!
-Yes.

388
00:27:51,269 --> 00:27:52,704
Since my family is in the police,

389
00:27:53,905 --> 00:27:56,741
everyone assumed
I'd become a police officer.

390
00:27:59,744 --> 00:28:03,515
Maybe I was just being rebellious,
thinking back on it now.

391
00:28:06,751 --> 00:28:08,153
Did you actually paint?

392
00:28:09,220 --> 00:28:10,055
Well…

393
00:28:12,057 --> 00:28:14,559
I painted portraits of the person I liked.

394
00:28:18,296 --> 00:28:19,197
It's embarrassing, isn't it?

395
00:28:20,098 --> 00:28:20,999
Man…

396
00:28:23,234 --> 00:28:24,402
It's lovely.

397
00:28:26,371 --> 00:28:29,474
Where did you learn to paint?

398
00:28:29,541 --> 00:28:31,342
No, my parents were strict…

399
00:28:35,113 --> 00:28:37,515
<i>There are people in this world</i>
<i>who have no dirt on them.</i>

400
00:28:39,084 --> 00:28:41,753
‎TAISUKE SAKURA

401
00:28:49,561 --> 00:28:52,130
<i>I don't like the fact that</i>
<i>he's keeping tabs on me, but…</i>

402
00:28:56,067 --> 00:28:58,169
<i>if Mariko can be happy,</i>

403
00:28:59,571 --> 00:29:00,972
<i>that's all that matters.</i>

404
00:29:07,245 --> 00:29:09,814
Is there perhaps someone else?

405
00:29:12,851 --> 00:29:16,855
Someone else you're interested in
or someone you're close with?

406
00:29:21,359 --> 00:29:22,827
Ah, I'm sorry.

407
00:29:22,894 --> 00:29:24,429
I've asked something strange.

408
00:29:25,396 --> 00:29:26,865
No, not at all.

409
00:29:35,640 --> 00:29:37,408
<i>If Mariko is happy,</i>

410
00:29:38,309 --> 00:29:39,778
<i>that's all that matters.</i>

411
00:30:05,270 --> 00:30:07,438
Sakura? Is something wrong?

412
00:30:08,807 --> 00:30:10,141
Oh, no.

413
00:30:10,708 --> 00:30:11,743
Let's go.

414
00:30:33,231 --> 00:30:35,033
-Here you are.
-Thank you very much.

415
00:30:35,099 --> 00:30:36,334
-Thank you.
-Thank you very much.

416
00:30:40,471 --> 00:30:41,406
Thank you.

417
00:30:51,416 --> 00:30:56,821
<i>There are people other than me</i>
<i>who can protect Mariko.</i>

418
00:31:00,825 --> 00:31:02,694
-Unrequited love?
-Right.

419
00:31:02,760 --> 00:31:05,263
If someone had held
an unrequited crush for you

420
00:31:05,330 --> 00:31:07,465
for a very long time,
Izumi, how would you feel?

421
00:31:08,166 --> 00:31:09,901
What's this all of a sudden?

422
00:31:09,968 --> 00:31:14,405
Ah, an acquaintance asked me
for advice about a problem.

423
00:31:15,707 --> 00:31:18,042
I think I'd be glad.

424
00:31:18,109 --> 00:31:21,679
It sounds like a shojo manga.
"I've always loved you, all along."

425
00:31:21,746 --> 00:31:23,848
It's quite heart-fluttering. Right, Sara?

426
00:31:23,915 --> 00:31:25,884
Yes, heart-fluttering.

427
00:31:25,950 --> 00:31:26,818
Heart-fluttering.

428
00:31:26,885 --> 00:31:29,487
Right! Girls definitely
think that way, don't they?

429
00:31:29,554 --> 00:31:30,788
It depends on the person.

430
00:31:30,855 --> 00:31:33,258
It's not like all girls think
the exact same way.

431
00:31:33,324 --> 00:31:35,026
Tomoya got scolded.

432
00:31:35,793 --> 00:31:38,129
Hey, that was not
getting scolded just now.

433
00:31:40,365 --> 00:31:41,266
All right, done!

434
00:31:41,332 --> 00:31:43,468
Mama, can I ride now?

435
00:31:43,534 --> 00:31:45,136
Sure, be careful.

436
00:31:45,203 --> 00:31:46,437
-Okay!
-Okay.

437
00:31:46,504 --> 00:31:47,438
See you.

438
00:31:49,107 --> 00:31:50,141
Be careful.

439
00:31:54,012 --> 00:31:55,513
Still, you know,

440
00:31:56,281 --> 00:31:59,417
that's assuming those feelings
remain pure, right?

441
00:32:01,552 --> 00:32:02,921
That unrequited love you mentioned.

442
00:32:04,856 --> 00:32:08,693
Love is always pure
at the beginning, isn't it?

443
00:32:09,827 --> 00:32:13,765
Just being able to see their face
from afar brings happiness.

444
00:32:13,831 --> 00:32:16,801
Just sharing the same space
brings happiness.

445
00:32:17,936 --> 00:32:21,906
But eventually, you inevitably start
wanting something in return.

446
00:32:23,207 --> 00:32:25,543
When you can't get it,

447
00:32:25,610 --> 00:32:27,845
yet you can't pull away
from the other person,

448
00:32:28,479 --> 00:32:31,482
wouldn't it feel like
it's become an obsession?

449
00:32:33,618 --> 00:32:34,953
-An obsession…
-Yes.

450
00:32:36,821 --> 00:32:40,224
But what about a guy
who's stayed in love forever

451
00:32:41,426 --> 00:32:42,727
without asking for anything

452
00:32:43,494 --> 00:32:46,731
and simply wishes for her happiness,
even if it remains unrequited?

453
00:32:46,798 --> 00:32:49,233
It might not be impossible.

454
00:32:49,834 --> 00:32:51,836
But it's not likely, isn't it?

455
00:32:53,237 --> 00:32:55,206
Hey, who is this about?

456
00:32:56,908 --> 00:32:58,743
Hey, welcome.

457
00:32:58,810 --> 00:33:01,746
-I want to go play.
-You're playing right now.

458
00:33:01,813 --> 00:33:05,149
She's been saying she wants to go
to an amusement park for a while now.

459
00:33:05,216 --> 00:33:06,684
Should we go together?

460
00:33:06,751 --> 00:33:08,653
What, seriously? Are you sure?

461
00:33:08,720 --> 00:33:10,688
I want to go to an amusement park too.

462
00:33:10,755 --> 00:33:13,191
Once you become an adult,
you don't get the chance to go.

463
00:33:13,925 --> 00:33:14,792
Want to go to the amusement park together?

464
00:33:14,859 --> 00:33:15,960
-Let's go!
-Yes.

465
00:33:16,027 --> 00:33:18,062
Really? Thank you!

466
00:33:18,129 --> 00:33:20,765
Should we practice
riding roller coasters, then?

467
00:33:20,832 --> 00:33:22,200
-Yes!
-Yes, let's do it.

468
00:33:22,266 --> 00:33:23,801
What is this, a squid?

469
00:33:23,868 --> 00:33:25,603
-Yes!
-Where is this from?

470
00:33:25,670 --> 00:33:26,504
Here?

471
00:33:26,571 --> 00:33:28,139
This is scary, you know.

472
00:33:35,847 --> 00:33:37,582
Wait, wait, break!

473
00:33:38,950 --> 00:33:40,418
-It's okay if I use this?
-Yes.

474
00:33:40,952 --> 00:33:43,321
I'll wash it
and give it back to you, then.

475
00:33:48,960 --> 00:33:50,361
-Hey.
-Huh?

476
00:33:51,295 --> 00:33:53,364
Why don't we try dating?

477
00:33:55,900 --> 00:33:57,835
I think it sounds good. What do you think?

478
00:34:02,540 --> 00:34:05,777
Mama, Tomoya!

479
00:34:05,843 --> 00:34:06,911
Hi!

480
00:34:19,757 --> 00:34:21,692
MARIKO

481
00:34:24,695 --> 00:34:28,633
I WENT TO AN ART MUSEUM TODAY

482
00:34:45,950 --> 00:34:49,087
Mariko, is now a good time
to discuss the marketing slogan?

483
00:34:49,153 --> 00:34:49,987
Yes.

484
00:34:50,555 --> 00:34:53,024
I've thought of a few…

485
00:34:53,091 --> 00:34:54,959
Don't you know?

486
00:34:56,494 --> 00:35:00,731
Mariko seems serious
about getting married.

487
00:35:02,500 --> 00:35:05,837
-At this rate--
-She always gets what she wants.

488
00:35:08,473 --> 00:35:10,408
So you do understand!

489
00:35:15,746 --> 00:35:17,115
-Try it like this.
-Okay.

490
00:35:17,815 --> 00:35:19,383
-Now enter.
-Okay.

491
00:35:19,917 --> 00:35:22,053
SEARCHING

492
00:35:22,653 --> 00:35:23,921
Wow, seriously!

493
00:35:23,988 --> 00:35:26,424
AI is searching the data for me.

494
00:35:26,491 --> 00:35:27,859
It's been updated so much.

495
00:35:27,925 --> 00:35:29,827
Right? It's great.

496
00:35:30,962 --> 00:35:31,796
Mariko!

497
00:35:32,497 --> 00:35:33,965
Thank you so much.

498
00:35:36,234 --> 00:35:40,371
The system getting updated
was thanks to you, wasn't it, Mariko?

499
00:35:41,272 --> 00:35:42,773
Huh? Why?

500
00:35:42,840 --> 00:35:44,742
We heard it from Yukimura.

501
00:35:44,809 --> 00:35:47,512
He said you made a suggestion
to the company.

502
00:35:48,012 --> 00:35:52,517
You said we should get the latest AI
to reduce the burden on employees, right?

503
00:35:53,351 --> 00:35:58,256
Besides that, there are so many things
you've been quietly doing for us

504
00:35:58,322 --> 00:36:02,226
that we didn't realize
until Yukimura told us.

505
00:36:02,894 --> 00:36:05,062
The reason you have
so many enemies in the company

506
00:36:06,164 --> 00:36:09,467
-is because you're fighting for us.
-Wait, wait, wait!

507
00:36:09,534 --> 00:36:11,135
-Shut up!
-What?

508
00:36:12,003 --> 00:36:13,604
I'm sorry.

509
00:36:13,671 --> 00:36:14,739
Okay, next, here.

510
00:36:15,306 --> 00:36:16,274
Okay.

511
00:36:25,449 --> 00:36:29,620
Yukimura really understands you,
doesn't he, Mariko?

512
00:36:31,756 --> 00:36:34,158
Is it all right to leave things
as they are now?

513
00:36:35,059 --> 00:36:35,893
What?

514
00:36:35,960 --> 00:36:38,663
I thought he might be
one of the rare people

515
00:36:38,729 --> 00:36:42,066
you actually open your heart to.

516
00:36:44,735 --> 00:36:47,405
When you're with him, it feels right.

517
00:36:48,206 --> 00:36:50,741
You don't always get to meet
someone like that, you know.

518
00:37:21,439 --> 00:37:22,473
‎I hate this…

519
00:37:45,596 --> 00:37:46,564
Good morning.

520
00:37:47,932 --> 00:37:51,969
Um, do you have time after work today?

521
00:37:54,572 --> 00:37:56,173
Yes, I do.

522
00:37:59,543 --> 00:38:03,414
There's a place I want to go with you.

523
00:38:14,759 --> 00:38:16,594
Careful when I close the door.

524
00:38:23,934 --> 00:38:26,270
It sways quite a bit, doesn't it?

525
00:38:36,447 --> 00:38:38,949
Wait! Please stop that.

526
00:38:39,016 --> 00:38:42,320
What? I just moved in my seat a little.

527
00:38:47,858 --> 00:38:51,162
Hey! You definitely did that
on purpose just now!

528
00:38:51,829 --> 00:38:54,231
Ah, seriously, stop. This sucks.

529
00:38:54,298 --> 00:38:55,933
So this is the kind of person you are.

530
00:38:56,000 --> 00:38:58,035
You get scared way too easily.

531
00:38:58,102 --> 00:38:59,203
This is my first time on a Ferris wheel.

532
00:38:59,270 --> 00:39:01,205
I didn't know it swayed this much…

533
00:39:02,006 --> 00:39:02,840
Hey!

534
00:39:02,907 --> 00:39:04,709
Stop…

535
00:39:04,775 --> 00:39:06,510
I didn't do anything.

536
00:39:07,311 --> 00:39:08,145
What?

537
00:39:08,713 --> 00:39:11,682
Ah, is it okay if I switch seats?

538
00:39:11,749 --> 00:39:13,084
No, don't move!

539
00:39:13,150 --> 00:39:14,218
-What?
-Please stop.

540
00:39:14,285 --> 00:39:15,319
I can't do this?

541
00:39:16,287 --> 00:39:17,822
Where should I sit?

542
00:39:17,888 --> 00:39:19,690
Huh? I wonder where?

543
00:39:20,458 --> 00:39:24,729
I thought you were a hero of justice,
but you can be a bully too, huh?

544
00:39:26,664 --> 00:39:29,934
Because you're funny.

545
00:39:32,036 --> 00:39:33,838
Huh? It stopped?

546
00:39:35,973 --> 00:39:39,076
Did you moving cause
the safety mechanism to trigger?

547
00:39:39,143 --> 00:39:41,812
-No, it's moving little by little.
-Hey…

548
00:39:42,947 --> 00:39:43,781
Look.

549
00:39:45,783 --> 00:39:47,017
Oh, my mistake.

550
00:39:49,854 --> 00:39:52,656
Hey, it's so pretty!

551
00:39:55,226 --> 00:39:57,495
Something flashed just now! What is that?

552
00:39:57,561 --> 00:39:58,829
An unidentified flying object?

553
00:39:59,597 --> 00:40:01,432
-No way.
-No, it is a UFO, for sure!

554
00:40:01,499 --> 00:40:02,767
Look over there!

555
00:40:02,833 --> 00:40:05,069
-It's flashing. It's flashing!
-Where?

556
00:40:05,136 --> 00:40:06,837
-Over there!
-What?

557
00:40:06,904 --> 00:40:09,206
-Some strange light! You can't see it?
-I can't see it.

558
00:40:09,273 --> 00:40:10,207
It's right there!

559
00:40:10,274 --> 00:40:11,776
-Where are you pointing?
-Right there!

560
00:40:11,842 --> 00:40:12,910
Where?

561
00:40:13,511 --> 00:40:14,612
Ah…

562
00:40:17,014 --> 00:40:17,915
I'm sorry.

563
00:40:25,322 --> 00:40:27,091
A UFO, huh?

564
00:40:27,925 --> 00:40:29,260
You're like a kid, surprisingly.

565
00:40:29,326 --> 00:40:31,695
No, I'm telling you it was there.

566
00:40:31,762 --> 00:40:33,197
You didn't see it?

567
00:40:34,165 --> 00:40:35,733
I feel bad for you.

568
00:40:41,772 --> 00:40:43,574
Ferris wheels are fun, aren't they?

569
00:40:45,376 --> 00:40:47,478
It's much more fun
than the last time I came here.

570
00:40:51,982 --> 00:40:53,484
Thank you for today.

571
00:40:54,852 --> 00:40:56,821
No, I was the one who invited you.

572
00:40:57,354 --> 00:40:58,456
It was a dream of mine.

573
00:41:00,424 --> 00:41:01,559
You're exaggerating again.

574
00:41:02,660 --> 00:41:04,295
I've dreamt of this.

575
00:41:07,264 --> 00:41:08,232
What?

576
00:41:09,033 --> 00:41:13,037
Well, if you wanted it so badly,
you should have come sooner.

577
00:41:14,972 --> 00:41:16,407
Bet you wanted to be here
with a certain someone.

578
00:41:16,474 --> 00:41:17,641
No…

579
00:41:43,701 --> 00:41:46,504
YUKIMURA SOTA

580
00:41:54,612 --> 00:42:01,552
GRADUATED FROM FUTABASHI UNIVERSITY
WENT TO MAKA HIGH SCHOOL

581
00:42:03,020 --> 00:42:05,856
MARIKO NOSE - YUKIMURA SOTA

582
00:42:05,923 --> 00:42:10,060
GRADUATED FROM FUTABASHI UNIVERSITY
WENT TO MAKA HIGH SCHOOL

583
00:42:20,404 --> 00:42:22,506
Well, this is where we part ways.

584
00:42:23,874 --> 00:42:24,708
Yes.

585
00:44:01,171 --> 00:44:02,206
Mariko!

586
00:44:06,210 --> 00:44:07,878
What? What's up?

587
00:44:09,413 --> 00:44:11,915
It's you, Mariko.

588
00:44:15,219 --> 00:44:18,489
The person I wanted to ride
the Ferris wheel with… It's you.

589
00:44:20,991 --> 00:44:22,326
I…

590
00:44:28,132 --> 00:44:29,133
I…

591
00:44:31,268 --> 00:44:32,202
I've always…

592
00:44:58,595 --> 00:45:03,534
‎NEXT TIME

593
00:45:08,105 --> 00:45:08,939
‎Subtitle translation by: Maslin Friedman
